<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">The question the whole year is about</div>
  <p class="cu-statement">How do you live well on a changing Earth?</p>
  <p>Every unit comes back to it. The short version of the answer this course is building toward: <strong>living well on a changing Earth requires deciding what to trust, what to protect, and what to give up.</strong> Those three decisions are what the units below take turns on.</p>
</div>

<h2>Why this page exists</h2>

<p>Most of what you do in this course is designed to transfer. You build a habitability framework in Unit 1 from planets you have been taught, then use it on a planet nobody has taught you. You learn OPVL in Unit 0 on news articles and use the same four letters in Unit 4 on climate projections. Every unit ends with you defending something in front of an audience that is not your teacher.</p>

<p>None of that was written down anywhere. This page writes it down. It is not new content and it does not change any assignment. It names the shape that was already there, so you can see what a unit is actually for while you are in the middle of it.</p>

<h2>The four threads</h2>

<p>A thread is something that does not belong to one unit. It starts somewhere, gets harder, and keeps coming back. These four are the ones named in <a href="/foundations/welcome/">Welcome to the Year</a>; the numbering below is the one the unit pages already use.</p>

